# tighConaillRescue -- the champion, half-drowned, in Conall's cabin
#
# Plays in six parts (tighConaill.js, _dream and _run). Every node closes the conversation; the scene plays
# them with _talk(1, n), and the actions are the scene's:
#   node 0 -- in the dark: black screen, soft rain, the drowning, "Lie still."   (the eyes then open)
#   node 1 -- "I was drowning" / "Thou art weary, nothing more."
#            [he crosses to the window; tighConaill.dlg "the better part of two days", as he draws the curtain]
#            [he comes back to the bed]
#   node 2 -- "Where is this place?" / "Thou art my guest. I am Conall."
#            [the brooch is tossed onto the clothes]
#   node 3 -- the mark: "Student of Dún Scáthach wear these. This one is for you."
#   node 4 -- "I bring no cattle" ... "the path of the blade,"
#            [he goes to the door and opens it; a pause]
#   node 5 -- at the door: "Is that not why all Gaelic Chieftains come to Skye?"   [the pause; out]
#
# IRISH IS A FIRST DRAFT -- check before shipping.

@file skye/tighConaill
@encounter 1


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — in the dark

> Drowning!
% Ag bá!
> I am in the grip of black water,
% Tá mé i ngreim ag an uisce dubh,
> It fills my throat.
% líonann sé mo scornach.

< Lie still.
% Bí socair.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 1 — half-woken

> I was drowning. I was surely drowning.
% Bhí mé ag bá. Bhí mé báite gan amhras.

< Thou art weary, nothing more.
% Níl ort ach tuirse.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 2 — where is this place

> Where is this place?
% Cá bhfuil mé anois?

< Thou art my guest. I am Conall.
% Mo aoi thú. Conall is ainm dom.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 3 — the mark
< Students wear the brooch of Skye. 
% Chaitheann daltaí dealg an Cheo.

< This one is for you.
% Duitse an ceann seo.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 4 — the path of the blade

> I brought no cattle with me,
% Níor thugas liom eallach, 


> nor fine tribute of silver.
% ná tiarnas breá airgid.

< Be still
% Bí socair

< Thou hast made thy case already upon the shore, senseless and half-drowned,
% Rinne tú do chás cheana féin nuair a bhain tú amach an trá, gan aithne, leathbáite,
< with the sea still running from thee.
% agus an fharraige fós ag sileadh uait.
< Take thy rest,
% Lig do scíth,
< Then shall I set thee on the path of the blade,
% Ansin cuirfidh mé ar bhóthar an chlaímh thú,


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 5 — at the door
Is that not why all Gaelic Chieftains come to Skye?
% Nach é sin a tógann na Taoisigh Gaelach ar fad go Cheo?
